10. Automated CV to JD screening engine
• Parse CVs with pypdf and python-docx (reuse existing extraction where present). Extract name, email, phone, education, qualifications, passing year, skills, experience, projects, certifications. Validate readability, supported format, duplicates (by email/phone/hash) and existing candidates. Show clear errors for bad files. Store files in a private directory, never publicly served.
• Parse JDs (PDF/DOCX/TXT) with jd_reader.py extended as needed, and show extracted fields for recruiter verification before saving.
• Extend skill_matcher.py without removing existing behaviour. Handle synonyms (for example 'JS' and 'JavaScript') and optional LLM-assisted semantic matching, always with a deterministic fallback.
• Configurable, documented weights (default): required skills 40%, experience 25%, qualification 15%, preferred skills 10%, certifications/other 10%. Show Overall, Skills, Qualification and Experience match, Matching Skills, Missing Required Skills, and a plain-language explanation.
• Unknown or missing information is treated as unknown, not negative (exclude it and renormalise weights). Do not use or infer protected attributes, names or photos in scoring. Save the criteria version used with every result.
• Threshold shortlisting is automatic. Below threshold = 'Needs Review' with recruiter override. No automatic rejection from a score.
11. Automated Level 1 phone interview engine
Architecture (modular adapters): campaign queue, call scheduler, telephony adapter, real-time media websocket, VAD plus streaming STT, interview orchestrator (state machine plus LLM), streaming TTS, recorder/transcriber, evaluator, notifier. Each piece is replaceable.
Campaign automation. When a campaign starts, create an interview plan per candidate (generated from the JD and CV, stored and editable by the recruiter before or after). Calls are queued and placed automatically inside the allowed calling window with a concurrency limit. Retries: configurable (default 2 retries, at least 4 hours apart). The recruiter can retry manually. Never call outside the window, never exceed the limit, never call without a verified application and campaign authorisation.
Call flow.
1.  Place the call. Validate provider webhook signatures. Track statuses: queued, ringing, answered, voicemail, no-answer, busy, failed, completed, declined, consent-denied.
2.  Identity check: 'Hello! Am I speaking with [Name]?' If it is not the candidate, reveal nothing about the application, apologise and end.
3.  Disclosure and consent: 'My name is Aira, the virtual AI recruitment assistant from [Company]. I'm calling about your application for [Job Title]. This is an AI-assisted preliminary interview and, with your permission, it will be recorded and transcribed. Do I have your permission to proceed?' Also offer language choice (English/Hindi) and a human-recruiter alternative. If declined, end politely, log the consent outcome and flag the candidate for recruiter follow-up. Without consent, do not record or transcribe.
4.  Voicemail or answering machine: hang up, log it, do not leave candidate details.
Interview stages (Aira follows the plan, not a fixed script): 1 Introduction and readiness; 2 Education and certifications; 3 Professional experience and projects; 4 Job-specific technical questions generated from the JD at the candidate's level (for example for a Python role: lists vs tuples, inheritance, exception handling, SQL joins); 5 Scenario-based problem solving; 6 Job-relevant communication (never judge accent, voice or speaking style); 7 Availability (notice period, joining date, expected salary and location preference only when relevant); 8 Candidate's questions (answer only from approved company information, otherwise say the team will follow up); 9 Warm closing: 'Thank you for your time. It was a pleasure speaking with you. Our recruitment team will review your interview and update you about the next steps.'
Dynamic conversation. The orchestrator tracks stage, questions asked and answers given. After each answer the LLM returns structured JSON (action: ask, follow_up, clarify, advance, repeat, end; text; reason) which is validated. Maximum 2 follow-ups per question, no repeated questions, off-topic answers redirected politely.
Real-time voice behaviour. Barge-in (stop speaking when the candidate starts), natural turn-taking, end-of-speech detection tuned to avoid cutting people off, silence handling (re-prompt after about 6s, 'Are you still there?', end after repeated silence), unclear speech ('Sorry, could you say that again?'), dropped calls and reconnection, hard time limit (default 15 minutes, gentle wrap-up at 13), immediate stop if the candidate asks. Target median response latency under 1.5 seconds. Stream TTS audio rather than waiting for full responses. Measure and report latency.
Web Interview (test mode / accessible alternative). Same orchestrator, running in the browser with microphone, the Aira avatar speaking with real audio-driven lip-sync, and a text-only option. Secure expiring link per candidate.
Failures. On any failure, set a truthful status ('Interview Failed', 'Missed Call', and so on), notify the recruiter, and allow a recruiter-controlled retry. Never produce an evaluation for an interview that did not run.
12. Interview evaluation and report
• Transcribe, then evaluate with a role-specific, configurable rubric: Technical Knowledge, Job-Relevant Experience, Problem-Solving, Communication (content and clarity only), Role-Specific Knowledge, Qualification Relevance. Score each 1 to 5 with transcript evidence. The evaluator may only cite what was actually said. Run a validation pass to catch unsupported claims.
• Output: strengths, areas needing clarification, recommended follow-up questions, completion status, duration, questions and answers, and a recommendation: Recommended for Recruiter Review, Needs Further Evaluation, or Not Yet Recommended. This is advice only. The recruiter decides.
• Generate a downloadable PDF report (candidate and job details, summary, question-wise evaluation, skills assessment, overall assessment, recruiter notes, next-step recommendation). Use an existing PDF library if present, otherwise propose the lightest one.
• Update candidate status through valid transitions only, write the audit trail, and notify the recruiter.
